{"change_summary":"Closed the remaining molt/mineral amendments by leaving the named critical GH hard-fail cutoff wired through the shrimp parameter path, preserving zeroed adult stage timers for processed `AddShrimp` save/load roundtrips instead of reapplying the legacy population timer, and verifying that cold-water and reserve-limited molt diagnostics are exercised through dedicated failure/stress regressions. I also removed the now-unused duplicate molt-condition helper after the breakdown-based diagnostics path became authoritative.","outstanding_risks":[],"steps":[{"description":"Verified the shrimp runtime, save/load, and event-diagnostic paths implicated by the pending amendments, then aligned the remaining regression expectations with the actual cold-readiness and processed-add-shrimp behavior.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Kept legacy molt-timer backfill scoped to truly legacy saves while preserving zero adult stage timers after processed shrimp additions, and retained the breakdown-driven molt diagnostics path without the dead helper wrapper.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Updated the cold-temperature and reserve-shortfall event tests so they hit real molt-resolution conditions and confirm the save/load roundtrip stays at zero for newly added adults.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran targeted regressions plus the full `tank_core`, `tank_data`, and `tank_scenarios` suites to confirm the amended molt/save-load behavior end to end.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all`","`cargo test -p tank_core --test validation -- --nocapture`","`cargo test -p tank_core --test save_load -- --nocapture`","`cargo test -p tank_core --test molt_mineral_budget -- --nocapture`","`cargo test -p tank_core --test events -- --nocapture`","`cargo test -p tank_core`","`cargo test -p tank_data`","`cargo test -p tank_scenarios`"]}